{"content":[{"c":["OLD GATE"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Jerusalem gate repaired by Joiada and Meshullam under Nehemiah’s supervision (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.3.6","r":"Neh.3.6","rawR":"Neh.3.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.3.6","value":"Neh.3.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 3:6"},"), and subsequently mentioned in the northerly route traveled by one of the companies of celebrants during the Jerusalem wall’s dedication (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.39","r":"Neh.12.39","rawR":"Neh.12.39","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.39","value":"Neh.12.39"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:39"},"). The Old Gate was located in the city’s northern wall between the Fish Gate and the Gate of Ephraim (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.38-39","r":"Neh.12.38-39","rawR":"Neh.12.38-39","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.38-39","value":"Neh.12.38-39"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:38-39"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Jerusalem_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Jerusalem_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Jerusalem_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Jerusalem"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"OldGate","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Neh 3:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.3.6","rawQueryValue":"Neh.3.6","sourceRefExact":"Neh.3.6"},{"anchorText":"12:39","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.39","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.39","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.39"},{"anchorText":"12:38-39","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.38-39","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.38-39","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.38-39"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"c07bc35da6fe7b6aea029411a0b83d581fd6660a2486e8da721f3caf099062a6","sourceItemName":"OldGate","sourceItemOrder